From 61494075165daf62651a2318919c8a1cf523174c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:42:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): review_required refusals name the
 operator rule; refuse before the goal judge

Follow-up to PR #1123 (deferred non-blocking review points, card t_01a1d11f2b89d33f):

1. edit_operator_fields refuses disabling review_required for every kanban
   worker run (HERMES_KANBAN_TASK / HERMES_KANBAN_WORKER_TASK), dispatched
   orchestrators included, but said "only an orchestrator". It now says "an
   operator (outside a kanban worker run)". require_review gives a worker
   approving a child pending in review without claiming it the same rule.
   Permission is unchanged; the rule is documented in the module docstring
   and the kanban CLI docs.
2. _handle_complete checks review_required before _goal_gate, so a goal_mode
   + review_required implementer gets the deterministic refusal without a
   judge call.
3. An operator (no worker identity) completing a review_required card outside
   review (CLI complete, dashboard done) is pointed at
   `hermes kanban edit <id> --review-required off` instead of the
   implementer-only kanban_request_review text.

Proof: tests/tools/test_kanban_review_required_wording.py (9) + updated
plumbing assertion: 9 fail on base 7755ecfca2, all pass on head; the
non-required goal-judge control passes on both. 33 affected test files
(744 tests) green; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
